# Not needed for the standard deployment anymore. The backend now
# serves this frontend's built files directly from the same origin
# (see backend/server.js and the root render.yaml), so relative /api
# calls just work in both dev (via Vite's proxy in vite.config.ts)
# and production (same server, same origin).
#
# Only set this if you're deliberately running the frontend and
# backend as separate services again (not recommended -- this is
# exactly the setup that made the login cookie a third-party cookie
# and got silently blocked by Chrome/Safari). If you do:
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend-url/api
